WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.868
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
I'm happy you're here.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:04.901
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.467
Guys, I'm very excited
about this.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.200
It is Fleet Week
here in New York City.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.267
Yeah, it's that special time
of year when

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.934
3,000 members of the military
tell their Uber driver,

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:21.167
"Thank you for your service."

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:23.968
And this is great.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:25.567
Tonight, our entire audience
is filled with

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.300
service members
of the U.S. military.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:34.767
♪♪

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.334
That's exa-- Looking good.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.534
This is a
very interesting crowd.

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.000
You're the only people
who watched Tom Cruise

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.767
fly upside down at 1,000 miles
per hour and go, "Boring."

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.634
I remember telling my dad
I thought I could be

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:51.033
a good soldier, and to this day,
it's still the hardest

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:52.367
I've ever made him laugh.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:53.934
Yeah.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.267
But this is cool.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:57.167
For Fleet Week, the public
can actually take tours of

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.934
some of the Navy ships
in the Hudson River.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.400
New Yorkers
are the only people who see

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.467
six beds crammed in a tiny room
and go, "Ooh, spacious.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.601
That's $3,000 a month
here, yeah."

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.167
Yeah. It is Fleet Week,
and tonight's audience

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.067
is made up of
active-duty service members

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.100
from the Army...

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:20.801
...the Navy...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:23.767
...the Air Force...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:27.033
...Marines.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:29.901
...and Coast Guard.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:36.200
We are so grateful for
your service.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.267
We can't thank you enough.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:40.901
I'm sorry, sir.
Do you have a question?

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.434
-Yeah, you forgot about
one of the branches.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:44.567
-I did?

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:47.634
-Yeah, you forgot to
mention Space Force.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.734
-Oh, right. Are you with them?

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.934
-Yep.
-Well, I'm sorry.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.367
Thank you for your service.

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:56.434
-Oh, you don't have to thank us.
We haven't done anything yet.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.834
-What have you been doing?

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:04.434
-Mostly setting up our office,
doing lots of Staples runs,

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.901
setting up printers,
buying notepads.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.100
You know, that kind of stuff.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.734
Oh, and Zoom.
So many Zoom calls.

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:12.200
-Who are you Zooming with?

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.434
-Like, other people in
the Space Force.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.734
-What do you talk about?

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:19.501
-Like, what to do if someone
attacked us from space

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:20.934
and then what we're going to
get at Chipotle.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:21.934
-Yeah.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.200
Got it. Got it.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.834
And just out of curiosity,
what would you do

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.834
if someone did
attack us from space?

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:29.267
-I'd call in the experts.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:31.367
-Like the top people in
Space Force?

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:32.534
-No way.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:34.567
I'd call the Army, the Navy,
the Air Force,

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:35.968
the Marines, the Coast Guard.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:37.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.100
-Smart man.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.868
Give it up for
the Space Force, everybody.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.734
Space Force.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.801
Guys, let's get to
some news here.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:54.067
Today, a Carnival cruise ship
was visiting Turks and Caicos

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.834
when it caught on fire.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.968
On the plus side,
for the first time ever,

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.133
the ship is sterilized.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:04.501
Yeah, usually, when you feel a
burning sensation on a cruise,

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:05.734
it's right after
you spend an hour

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.634
with a stranger in the hot tub.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:08.901
Switching gears.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.234
Today, Disney
released a first look at

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.634
"Indiana Jones 5,"
starring Harrison Ford.

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:14.767
Check this out.

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:17.767
Hmm. Yeah, "Indiana Jones 5."

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:18.901
Although, based on the photo,

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.367
it looks more like
the sequel to "Hamilton."

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.367
Of course, you can tell
Indiana Jones is getting older

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.901
because before cracking
his whip, he has to take a pill.

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:31.968
Some more entertainment news.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.634
Guys, tomorrow,
the new "Star Wars" series,

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.567
"Obi-Wan Kenobi"
drops on Disney+.

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.667
I am pretty pumped.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.200
I'm excited about this.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.400
Tariq, you excited?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.400
-I guess, sure.
Obi-Wan Kenobi's okay.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.968
-Oh, you're not really
a "Star Wars" fan?

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.267
-No, I love "Star Wars."

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:54.000
What I'm saying is that there
are other members of

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.400
Obi-Wan Kenobi's family

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.300
that I'd probably rather
watch a show about.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.200
-Other members of his family?
Like who?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.200
-Like, well --
You know, I did some digging

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.334
on Wookieepedia.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.701
And he's got
lots of cool relatives,

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:12.033
Like his brothers,
the Opie-Wan Kenobi

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.601
and Tobey-Wan Maguire.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:16.667
And then there's his sisters,

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:20.834
Obi-Wanda Sykes and
Oprah-Wan Kenofrey.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:23.234
-Oprah-Wan Kenofrey?

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:24.367
Interesting, I've never
heard of those.

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:25.667
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:29.767
Well, then there are
his cousins, Abra-Wan Cadabra,

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:32.501
Oba-Barbara Ann,

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.400
ABBA Mamma Mia,

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.868
and O-Bologna Burrito.

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:36.868
-Okay.

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:38.567
-Oh, then you got the twins,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.801
Yabba-Dabba and
Scooby-Dooby-Doo.

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:44.334
And then there's
O-Bebop-and-Rocksteady.

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:46.634
O-Baby-Boss-Bumps-A-Baba.

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:47.834
-Okay, okay. You okay, bud?

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:50.334
-Oh, there's also

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:54.434
O-Barack-Obama-in-da-Bahamas-
wearing-llama-pajamas.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:58.334
And, of course,
O-bawitdaba-Da-Bang-Da-Bang-

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:01.734
Diggy-diggy-Diggy-
to-the-Boogie-Said-Up-Jump-the-

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:02.767
Kenobi.

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:04.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:07.934
-Is that it?

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.734
-I'm just kidding.
I've never seen "Star Wars."

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:10.868
-Alright.
Tariq Trotter, everyone.

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.267
Tariq Trotter.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:14.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:18.701
Well, guys, listen to this.

00:05:18.701 --> 00:05:21.400
A recent study found that men
who post shirtless photos

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.000
on dating apps are viewed as

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.734
less competent
and more promiscuous.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:28.801
I like the idea of people
looking at dating profiles like,

00:05:28.801 --> 00:05:30.100
"Well, he must be competent.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.934
He has a shirt."

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:34.567
Well, get this.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.767
A new poll found that
Trader Joe's

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:39.000
is the most reputable brand
in the country.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.667
Yeah, at Trader Joe's,

00:05:40.667 --> 00:05:42.133
you know exactly
what you're going to get --

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.634
hummus from a white guy
in dreadlocks.

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:47.767
I love Trader Joe's.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.667
It's like Whole Foods
if it took a gap year

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:52.133
to travel before college.

